Schema validation & Raw dictionaries reach the library without SDK schema validation. & Null, string, number, list and missing \texttt{inputSchema} variants all pass scanning, registration and invocation checks, contrary to documented malformed-schema denial. An ordinary object schema also passes. \\
Descriptor projection & The host consumes a top-level \texttt{title}; covered fields stay unchanged. & Changing only the title to the controlled denial marker preserves the fingerprint and permits invocation. The same marker in the covered description denies registration and invocation. This is a projection-scope observation. \\
Registration ordering & A separate actor mutates a shared descriptor after scanning but before fingerprinting; a test audit hook only schedules the interleaving. & The changed descriptor passes invocation although a fresh scan denies it. Copying the descriptor before registration makes the changed current descriptor fail invocation. This condition assumes shared mutable host state; thread safety is not promised. \\
Server namespace & One unnamespaced registry serves two trusted connections with identically named tools. & Registering B overwrites A; checking A denies it and then B. Distinct registries with copied descriptors permit both. This is an availability collision, not malicious dispatch. \\
